    <article>
        <articleInfo lang="EN" FirstPage="1" LastPage="43">
            <pdf>26301-jdecp-chernov.pdf</pdf>
            <abstract>We consider a game problem consisting in neutralization of perturbation of a semilinear evolutionary equation with nonstationary linear operator in a Hilbert space. We suppose that the right-hand side of equation depends linearly on two controls and one of them is treated as some perturbation while another is treated as the neutralizing action of the operating player. It is required to carry over the controlled system to a given state at a given time moment in the presence of perturbation. Both controls are supposed bounded by the norm. As is well known, in such a form one can present also pursuit games. We establish sufficient conditions for solvability of the determined game problem in both cases of linear and nonlinear equation. Here we use the Minty-Browder's theorem and also a chain technology of successive continuation of the solution to a controlled system to intermediate states. As example of reduction to the abstract operator equation under study we consider the semilinear equation of global electric circuit in the Earth atmosphere and a semilinear pseudoparabolic equation.</abstract>
            <title>On solvability of a game problem consisting in neutralization of perturbation of an evolution equation with a nonstationary operator</title>
            <keywords>
                <word>semilinear evolutionary equation in a Hilbert space</word>
                <word>nonstationary operator</word>
                <word>conditions for solvability of a game problem</word>
                <word>neutralization of perturbation</word>
            </keywords>
