        <articleInfo lang="EN" FirstPage="44" LastPage="83">
            <pdf>26302-jdecp-pranevich.pdf</pdf>
            <abstract>In this paper we consider real polynomial systems of partial differential equations of the first order. The method of building real first integrals and last multipliers by known real and complex-valued polynomial partial integrals, taking into account their multiplicity, and conditional partial integrals has been developed. The influence of Jacobian conditions on the possibility of constructing first integrals and last multipliers by partial integrals of partial differential system is shown. Functional relationships between the coordinate functions of cofactors of partial integrals of complete and Jacobian systems of partial differential equations are established. The problems of modifying first integrals and last multipliers of the Darboux type are solved. Sufficient conditions of constructing first integrals for partial differential systems by two known partial integrals are obtained. The possibility of constructing first integrals for normal partial differential systems by a known partial integral is considered. Examples of systems of partial differential equations of the first order are given, which illustrate the theoretical studies carried out in this article. The results can be applied in the analytical theory of differential equations and applied problems of mechanics, optics and hydrodynamics.</abstract>
            <title>Partial integrals of real polynomial partial differential systems of the first order</title>
            <keywords>
                <word>system of partial differential equations</word>
                <word>complete partial differential system</word>
                <word>Jacobian partial differential system</word>
                <word>first integral</word>
                <word>real partial integral</word>
                <word>complex-valued partial integral</word>
                <word>multiplicity</word>
                <word>conditional partial integral</word>
                <word>last multiplier</word>
                <word>last pseudo-multiplier</word>
            </keywords>
