    <article>
        <articleInfo lang="EN" FirstPage="84" LastPage="103">
            <pdf>26303-jdecp-hien.pdf</pdf>
            <abstract>In this paper, the problems of stability and stabilization via static output-feedback control are extended for positive continuous-time Roesser model described Caputo derivatives with incommensurate orders. A general solution representation to state-space equation of the model is first given. Then, using the established solution representation, necessary and sufficient conditions ensuring the positivity of the system (i.e. all system states initiated from nonnegative states are always nonnegative for all times) are derived. By utilizing the monotonicity induced from the positivity, a necessary and sufficient stability condition is formulated in terms of a tractable LP condition. The obtained stability result is then taken into deriving LP-based conditions for the existence of a desired controller that makes the closed-loop system positive and stable.</abstract>
            <title>Analysis and control of positive 2-D systems in continuous-time Caputo-Roesser model</title>
            <keywords>
                <word>Fractional-order 2-D systems</word>
                <word>positivity</word>
                <word>Roesser model</word>
                <word>linear programming</word>
            </keywords>
