            <pdf>26307-jdecp-vasilieva.pdf</pdf>
            <abstract>This paper presents sufficient conditions for the existence of a countable set of infinite uncountable invariant sets in the neighborhood of a non transversal homoclinic point of a diffeomorphism of the plane into itself. The trajectories of points of these sets lie in the extended neighborhood of the homoclinic trajectory.</abstract>
            <title>On the question of the structure of the neighborhood of a homoclinic point of a diffeomorphism of the plane. I.</title>
            <keywords>
                <word>hyperbolic point</word>
                <word>non-transverse homoclinic point</word>
                <word>stability</word>
                <word>stable and unstable manifold</word>
                <word>order of contact</word>
            </keywords>
