    <article>
        <articleInfo lang="EN" FirstPage="151" LastPage="166">
            <pdf>26308-jdecp-kayumov.pdf</pdf>
            <abstract>We consider the control of a two-link pendulum with an elastic joint, which moves in a horizontal plane under the action of a limited external torque applied at the first hinge. The pendulum is modeled by two rigid rods with a helical spring between them, unstressed in the straightened configuration. Kinematic constraints are not imposed on the system (constructively excluded), and friction is absent. The problem being solved is rotation the system through the largest angle in a given time from an initial rest state to a final one. Trajectories satisfying the necessary optimality conditions were numerically constructed. The evolution of the optimal control functions with changing the assigned motion time is demonstrated on a dedicated diagram. The results indicate that the problem of rotation the system by the largest angle in a given time is a mutual variational problem of the time-optimal turning by a given angle.</abstract>
            <title>Optimal turning of a flat two-link pendulum with an elastic joint</title>
            <keywords>
                <word>flat two-link pendulum with an elastic joint</word>
                <word>optimal control</word>
            </keywords>
            <references>
