                <reference>Avetisyan V.V., Bolotnik N.N., Chernous’ko F.L. Optimal program movements of a two-link manipulator. Izv. Akad. Nauk SSSR. Techn. kibernetika. 1985. No. 3. P. 123-131.</reference>
                <reference>Bolotnik N.N., Chernous’ko F.L. Optimization of control of manipulation robots. Izv. Akad. Nauk SSSR. Techn. kibernetika. 1990. No. 1. P. 189-238.</reference>
                <reference>Pontrjagin L.S., Boltjanskii V.G., Gamkrelidze R.V., Mishchenko E.F. Matematicheskaja teorija optimalnih processov [Mathematical theory of optimal processes]. Moscow, Nauka Publ., 1977. 392 p.</reference>
                <reference>Osipov S.N., Formal’skii A.M. The problem of the time-optimal turning of a manipulator. J. Appl. Math. Mech. 1988. Vol. 52, No 6. P. 725-731.</reference>
                <reference>Kayumov O.R. Time-optimal movement of a trolley with a pendulum. Journal of Computer and Systems Sciences International. 2021. Vol. 60, No 1. P. 28-38.</reference>
                <reference>Wittenburg G. Dinamika sistem tverdykh tel. [Dynamics of solid state systems]. Moscow, Mir Publ., 1980. 292 p.</reference>
                <reference>Kayumov O.R. Optimal movement of a platform with an inverted pendulum. Journal of Computer and Systems Sciences International. 2025. Vol. 64, No 6. P. 954-971.</reference>
                <reference>Kalman R.E. The general theory of control systems. Proc. 1st Int. Conf. IFAC, vol. 2. Izd. Acad. Nauk SSSR, Moscow. 1961. pp. 521–546.</reference>
                <reference>Kayumov O.R. On the global controllability of some lagrangian systems. Izv. Akad. Nauk SSSR. Mekh. Tverd. Tela. 1986. No. 6. P. 16–24.</reference>
                <reference>Chernous’ko F.L., Akulenko L.D., Sokolov B.N. Upravlenie kolebanijami [Oscillation control]. Moscow, Nauka Publ., 1980. 383 p.</reference>
                <reference>Kayumov O.R. Diagrams of Optimal Control Functions in the Problem of the Fastest Platform Movement with Two Oscillators. Journal of Computer and Systems Sciences International. 2022. Vol. 61, No 5. P. 776-792.</reference>
